WEBVTT

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.480
Keijo High School

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.480
Keijo, forward pass.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.990
Jinko's scrum.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.970
A scrum at the ten meter line!

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:30.860
This is our chance!

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:32.920
What's the ten meter line?

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.510
Did you actually study the rules?

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:44.150
When you look at a rugby field from above, 
you'll see a bunch of lines on the field.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:44.140
<b>Halfway Line</b>

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:44.140
<b>10m Line</b>

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.140
<b>22m Line</b>

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.140
<b>Goal Line</b>

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:57.530
<b>Halfway Line</b>

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:57.530
<b>10m Line</b>

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:57.530
<b>22m Line</b>

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:57.530
<b>Goal Line</b>

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:57.530
<b>Kan</b>

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:57.530
<b>Kei</b>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:49.050
Right now, we're at the
ten meter line on Keijo's half.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:51.500
Rugby is about securing 
your team's position.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:55.470
The deeper you are in the opponent's half, 
the more chances you'll have.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:00.270
Takebe-senpai.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.620
Come here.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.050
Bring it.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.590
Is #10 trying to pass me?

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.640
No, #12 will cross with the ball.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.440
I know exactly what you're up to!

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.410
Bzzt. Too bad.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.410
They got me.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.660
Quit messing with us!

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:51.070
<i>A pass to the right.</i>

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:57.400
Keep your eyes open, Ise!

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:01.390
You can throw the ball without looking?

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:05.640
Well, yeah.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.260
Oharano's so good.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.780
I heard he played in grade and
middle school, and at rugby school.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:13.770
It's no wonder.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:19.220
It won't work.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:09.470
<b>Episode 4
What Should I Do?</b>

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.970
Watch out for Jinko's #10!

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.230
A kick pass?

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.480
You idiot, Maroudo!

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.730
What? He couldn't catch that?

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.180
It won't work.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:25.400
Most of our players started 
playing rugby in high school.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.280
They're not used to playing 
with someone so good.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.370
He's good.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.870
But he's not a good player.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:35.460
Damn it.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.590
Th-Three guys?

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:51.180
Keijo is trying to shut down Oharano!

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.400
How will you handle this, first-year?

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.290
You can't do anything now!

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.280
Oharano, pass!

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:08.200
Three dudes? How uncomfortable.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.720
You've got to play smarter.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.640
A drop goal?

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:44.190
Does that score us points, too?

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:47.150
Yeah, but it's not often 
that you get to see that.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:57.160
Keijo

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:49.020
Wow.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:53.080
We just scored against
a Kanagawa Prefecture semifinalist.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:57.890
Damn, Jinko.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:01.670
You picked up some pretty good first-years.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:04.550
Miyuki.

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:08.690
I know.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:13.510
The drop goal caught me off guard, 
but that was just a lucky shot.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.330
I'll stop him from doing anything else.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:27.360
The first half is almost over.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.980
If we can keep this up...

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:33.730
That's not good enough.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.350
They're so fast! What was that?

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:44.380
They changed their defense.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:48.820
When they get that close, 
you don't even have time to think.

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:51.640
They're trying to keep us from passing.

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:56.600
Let's see which of us is more amazing.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:02.400
No way. Sounds uncomfortable.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:04.760
Hey, you truant thug.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:05.890
What?

00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:07.480
How can we win?

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:11.430
Is that how you should be asking 
that question, you little turd?

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:14.280
Just tell your dear little junior.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:16.950
Listen up.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:20.180
Even with a strong number eight
to get the ball

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.870
and a stand-off to carry it
where we need to go,

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:24.790
we don't have anyone to score a try.

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:28.870
We don't have a great wing on the field!

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:31.000
Oh, right.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.550
The first half is over!

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:44.810
I can't believe that first-year joined Jinko.

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:48.320
They'll be as easy to beat
as they always are.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:57.330
There's no such thing as a guaranteed win.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:04.630
We'll respect our opponents and 
crush them during the second half.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:06.940
Captain.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:17.350
Are you keeping the same lineup 
in for the second half?

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:21.640
There's no way, right?

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:26.150
Those shitty backs made tons of 
mistakes during the first half.

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:28.900
We won't win unless you put me in.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:32.560
Ebumi, you don't even show up to practice!

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:33.150
Huh?

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.290
You're right.

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:39.150
You do have a high rugby IQ.

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.250
Captain.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.160
You're the fastest man on the team.

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:45.130
That's right.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:48.920
If you use me, we'll score plenty of tries.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:52.130
But...

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:57.150
Don't tell me how to play rugby.

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:00.700
Rugby isn't a one-man sport.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:06.440
A player who doesn't sweat on the field 
doesn't deserve to receive passes.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:14.220
We won't be changing our lineup.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:18.850
Let's go get them.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:21.790
Seriously?! Dammit!

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.340
The game isn't over yet.

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:29.320
You'll play next time, right?

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:30.330
Don't run.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.230
Damn.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:38.820
The mood changed for the worse.

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:49.480
I'll stop him.

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:59.320
He passed over three guys?

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:01.120
Are they sending their wing through?

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:02.950
No.

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:05.700
It's Taira!

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.130
Why is a forward on the flank?

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:14.460
I'm wide open!

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:18.150
Now they pass to their wing?

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:26.030
Try!

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:34.060
Seriously?

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:36.490
Switch gears!

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:39.490
Taira's still on the flank.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.260
Be careful.

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:48.120
If you keep looking to the outside,

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:51.580
we'll go right through the middle!

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:56.310
Try!

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:00.210
They completely changed their tactics.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.720
They positioned one of their big guys
furthest on the flank

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.310
and are passing us with 
strength instead of speed.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:12.910
And when we gather
on the flank to stop them,

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:15.480
they pass us on our undermanned middle.

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:21.070
Try!

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:35.340
Try!

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:51.950
Suwa.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:56.850
I'm not sure he can play anymore.

00:11:58.220 --> 00:11:59.570
We'll have to sub in a wing.

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:01.420
S-Sub?

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:04.170
Seriously? Isn't that me?

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:05.930
I can't stop them!

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:07.790
I don't want to play!

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:08.430
Huh?

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:12.950
Yikes!

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:35.450
<i>Who...</i>

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.320
<i>can stop...</i>

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:54.490
<i>the flow of the game?</i>

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:09.930
Gion.

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:14.980
<b>Since our
wings are
named
"Yukichi"</b>

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:14.980
<b>and "Yoichi"
which are
fortuitous-
sounding
names...</b>

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.980
Five Thousand Yen                   Ten Thousand Yen

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:17.980
<b>Why don't
we call them
"The Profit
Wings?"</b>

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:17.980
<b>If you're
thinking
about that
during the
game, I'm
going to
hit you!</b>

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:17.980
It's kind of
funny, though

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:22.480
Gion, get changed.

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:29.240
All right!

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:30.990
What? No way.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:34.150
I-I didn't check, but do you have cleats?

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:35.250
What?

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:39.380
Come to think of it, the little guy 
gave me something on the way here.

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:47.880
Cleats and a jersey.

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:06.350
Good luck.

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:28.930
Hey.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:34.180
What should I do?

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:48.650
I only know how to tackle.

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:51.950
I don't even know how to play rugby.

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:54.530
But I want to win.

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:12.470
An idiot novice like you 
shouldn't overthink things.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:14.990
You've got only one job.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:19.850
Kill our opponents!

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:23.360
That's it?

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:28.380
That's easy.

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:32.480
Leave it to me.

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:35.780
I'll kill some guys for you, too.

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:39.910
Shut up! Just go!

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:41.210
All right!

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:59.210
Bring it on!

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:04.480
They sent someone pretty 
small onto the field.

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:07.480
<i>Don't call him short.</i>

00:16:20.940 --> 00:16:22.780
<i>Is he nervous?</i>

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:30.970
Five minutes left.

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:34.260
Will Gion be okay?

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:39.090
It's been only a week since 
he started playing rugby.

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:41.770
I-It's Taira again.

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:47.020
<i>Is he too scared to move?</i>

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:52.780
<i>So low!</i>

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:57.030
<i>I'll stab low, just like 
how I tackled the captain.</i>

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:12.840
We finally stopped him.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:14.590
Of course.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.590
My opponent is moving, too.

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:18.930
Damn it.

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:21.260
I'll stop him next time.

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:22.670
Gion.

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:27.480
Don't sweat the small stuff.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:28.940
Keep going for tackles.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:32.440
Yeah. Keep stabbing, Gion.

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:35.050
Your position isn't wing.

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:36.470
It's "Gion."

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:40.700
Yes, sir.

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:42.780
What is he doing?

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:47.210
Watch where you're going!

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.460
I won't let a first-year outdo me!

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:53.430
<i>Their aura changed?</i>

00:17:58.490 --> 00:18:00.100
Here comes #10!

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:14.020
<i>I'll get him this time.</i>

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:22.580
Gion-kun.

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:24.450
Go after him.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:31.210
Shut up, Iwashimizu! I know!

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:08.250
Try!

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:09.610
Damn!

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.900
I was so close, too.

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:26.260
It's the last play.

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:35.100
Gion, it's not over yet.

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:37.180
You score five points per try in rugby.

00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:39.650
You score two more with the kick after that.

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:44.430
But if we try hard enough, we can stop them
from scoring two points off the kick.

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:47.660
Run.

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:49.970
Let's go and get in their way.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:59.400
Run!

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:07.430
<i>I haven't done anything yet.</i>

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:40.950
No goal!

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:47.230
No side!

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:50.300
Dammit.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:55.530
I... I couldn't do anything.

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:59.020
You got me.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.010
Nice play.

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:04.530
What?

00:21:08.050 --> 00:21:09.490
Hold your head high.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:15.160
You stopped Taira, even if 
it was just for a second.

00:21:16.190 --> 00:21:20.300
With the time you gave us, 
we made it.

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:24.120
Good job chasing #10 until the end.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:27.550
By forcing them to score a try on the edge,

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:29.680
they had to take a kick 
from a difficult position.

00:21:31.230 --> 00:21:32.510
They missed it.

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:36.310
You did what you could.

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:40.090
Keep looking forward to your next game.

00:21:43.730 --> 00:21:44.550
Let's go line up.

00:21:55.450 --> 00:22:00.460
Next time, I'll definitely win!

00:22:07.770 --> 00:22:10.130
Good game!

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
<b>Next Time: "What's Lacking"</b>

00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:48.020
Next time: "What's Lacking."
